---
import SiteLayout from "../components/SiteLayout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "November 1, 2026";
---

<SiteLayout title="Terms - Lapis Notes">
  <main class="legal-main">
    <header class="legal-hero">
      <p class="landing-eyebrow">Terms</p>
      <h1>Terms</h1>
      <p class="legal-dek">
        These terms describe the basic rules for using the Lapis Notes website,
        documentation, web app, desktop app, and project resources.
      </p>
      <p class="legal-meta">Last updated {lastUpdated}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="legal-content">
      <section class="legal-section" aria-labelledby="agreement">
        <h2 id="agreement">Agreement</h2>
        <p>
          By using Lapis Notes or the lapis.md website, you agree to these
          terms, the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> page, and the open-source and
          content licenses that apply to the materials you use. If you do not agree,
          do not use the app or site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section" aria-labelledby="services">
        <h2 id="services">What Lapis Provides</h2>
        <p>
          Lapis Notes provides a local-first notes app, public documentation,
          source code, developer APIs, and project resources. The web app and
          desktop app are provided as software you run in your own browser or on
          your own device.
        </p>
        <p>
          Lapis does not currently provide hosted vault storage, hosted sync,
          accounts, subscriptions, or payment processing. If those services are
          added later, these terms and the privacy page should be updated before
          they are offered publicly.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section" aria-labelledby="your-content">
        <h2 id="your-content">Your Content And Responsibilities</h2>
        <p>
          You keep ownership of the notes, files, attachments, notebooks, and
          other content you create or open with Lapis Notes. You are responsible
          for your content, your backups, and your compliance with laws and
          third party rights that apply to your work.
        </p>
        <p>
          Do not use the app, site, or project infrastructure to harm systems,
          violate rights, distribute unlawful content, or interfere with other
          users or maintainers.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section" aria-labelledby="licenses">
        <h2 id="licenses">Licenses And Ownership</h2>
        <p>
          Lapis Notes is distributed under multiple licenses by package and
          content type. The license overview explains the core app, plugin API,
          docs, examples, third-party code, and trademark boundaries.
        </p>
        <div class="legal-links-row">
          <a class="site-button site-button--secondary" href="/license/"
            >Read the license overview</a
          >
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section" aria-labelledby="plugins">
        <h2 id="plugins">Plugins, Code Execution, And Third Parties</h2>
        <p>
          Plugins, notebook cells, embeds, links, package CDNs, model hosts, and
          other third-party services can execute code, load remote resources, or
          process data outside the core app. You are responsible for deciding
          what plugins and code to trust.
        </p>
        <p>
          Lapis is not responsible for third-party plugins, third-party
          services, or content reached through external links.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section" aria-labelledby="availability">
        <h2 id="availability">Availability And Changes</h2>
        <p>
          The app and site are provided as they are available. Features, routes,
          documentation, package boundaries, and distribution builds may change,
          be removed, or stop working. Static web hosting and third-party
          dependencies may also be unavailable from time to time.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section" aria-labelledby="disclaimer">
        <h2 id="disclaimer">No Warranties</h2>
        <p>
          Lapis Notes is provided "as is" and "as available" without warranties
          of any kind to the maximum extent allowed by law. The app may contain
          bugs, data loss risks, compatibility issues, security issues, or
          documentation errors.
        </p>
        <p>
          You should keep independent backups of important vaults and test
          workflows before relying on them for critical work.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section" aria-labelledby="liability">
        <h2 id="liability">Limitation Of Liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the maximum extent allowed by law, Lapis Notes contributors and
          maintainers are not liable for indirect, incidental, special,
          consequential, exemplary, or punitive damages, or for lost data, lost
          profits, business interruption, or security incidents arising from
          your use of the app, site, docs, plugins, or third-party services.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section" aria-labelledby="updates">
        <h2 id="updates">Updates To These Terms</h2>
        <p>
          The latest terms will be published on this page. Continued use of the
          app or site after changes means you accept the updated terms.
        </p>
        <div class="legal-links-row">
          <a class="site-button site-button--secondary" href="/privacy/"
            >Privacy</a
          >
          <a class="site-button site-button--secondary" href="/license/"
            >License</a
          >
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
